messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nBob is big. Bob is nice. Bob is smart. Charlie is nice. Dave is nice. Erin is big. Erin is blue. Erin is furry. Erin is quiet. Erin is round. Erin is smart. All nice things are big. All furry things are blue. Blue, furry things are quiet. If something is round and nice then it is blue. If Bob is round then Bob is blue. Big, quiet things are furry. If something is blue and furry then it is smart. If Charlie is nice and Charlie is big then Charlie is quiet.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Dave is big.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>.\nTo determine if the statement "Dave is big" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context, we need to carefully analyze the information provided and apply logical reasoning step by step.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - Bob is big.\n   - Bob is nice.\n   - Bob is smart.\n   - Charlie is nice.\n   - Dave is nice.\n   - Erin is big.\n   - Erin is blue.\n   - Erin is furry.\n   - Erin is quiet.\n   - Erin is round.\n   - Erin is smart.\n   - All nice things are big.\n   - All furry things are blue.\n   - Blue, furry things are quiet.\n   - If something is round and nice then it is blue.\n   - If Bob is round then Bob is blue.\n   - Big, quiet things are furry.\n   - If something is blue and furry then it is smart.\n   - If Charlie is nice and Charlie is big then Charlie is quiet.\n\n2.**Dave\'s Information:**.\n   - Dave is nice.\n\n3.**Checking Dave\'s Bigness:**.\n   - From the context, we know that all nice things are big.\n   - Since Dave is nice, by the rule "All nice things are big," we can conclude that Dave is big.\n\n4.**Conclusion:**.\n   - Based on the given information, Dave is indeed big.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Dave is big" is true.\n\nThe correct