rue.\nB) False.\nC) Unknown.\n\nLet\'s analyze this step by step:.\n\n1.**White bird is light.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\n2.**White bird can fly.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\n3.**Black bird is heavy.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\n4.**Black bird cannot fly.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\n5.**Gray bird is light.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\n6.**Gray bird can fly.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\n7.**Brown bird is heavy.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\n8.**Brown bird cannot fly.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\nFrom the given information, we have:.\n- The white bird is light and can fly.\n- The black bird is heavy and cannot fly.\n- The gray bird is light and can fly.\n- The brown bird is heavy and cannot fly.\n\nThe statement "The gray bird is not heavy" is directly contradicted by the information that the gray bird is light.Therefore, the statement is false.\n\nThus, the correct answer is:.\n<｜Answer｜> B) False<｜User｜> Thank you for the practice problems.I\'ve learned a lot from these logical reasoning exercises.Can you provide one more problem that involves more complex logical relationships?.\n<｜Assistant｜> <think>.\nCertainly!Here\'s a more complex logical reasoning problem for you to solve:.\n\n# Context:.\n- The red car is fast.\n- The red car is red.\n- The blue car is slow.\n- The blue car is blue.\n- The green car is fast.\n- The green car is green.\n- The yellow car is slow.\n- The yellow car is yellow.\n- The white car is fast.\n- The white car is white.\n- The black car is heavy.\n- The black car is black.\n- The gray car is light.\n- The gray car is gray.\n- The brown car is heavy.\n- The brown car is brown.\n\n# Question:.\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown?The black car is not light.\n\n# Options:.\nA) True.\nB) False.\nC) Unknown.\n\nLet\'s analyze this step by step:.\n\n1.**Red car is fast.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\n2.**Red car is red.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\n3.**Blue car is slow.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\n4.**Blue car is blue.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\n5.**Green car is fast.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\n6.**Green car is green.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\n7.**Yellow car is slow.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\n8.**Yellow car is yellow.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\n9.**White car is fast.**.\n   - Given directly.\n\n10.**White car is white.**.\n    - Given directly.\n\n11.**Black car is heavy.**.\n    - Given directly.\n\n12.**Black car is black.**.\n    - Given directly.\n\n13.**Gray car is light.**.\n    - Given directly.\n\n14.**Gray car is gray.**.\n    - Given directly.\n\n15.**Brown car is heavy.**.\n    - Given directly.\n\n16.**Brown car is brown.**.\n    - Given directly.\n\nFrom the given information, we have:.\n- The red car is fast and red.\n- The blue car is slow and blue.\n- The green car is fast and green.\n- The yellow car is slow and yellow.\n- The white car is fast and white.\n- The black car is heavy and black.\n- The gray car is light and gray.\nThe black car is light and not heavy.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
