k if Gary can be quiet and green simultaneously.\n\n4.**Checking for Contradictions:**.\n   - If Gary is quiet, then by the statement "Quiet, green things are not red," Gary would need to be green.\n   - But we also know that "All quiet, kind things are not white." Since Gary is quiet and not red, he cannot be white, which contradicts the statement that all quiet, kind things are not white.\n\n5.**Conclusion:**.\n   - The contradiction indicates that Gary cannot be both quiet and green.\n   - Therefore, Gary cannot be quiet.\n\nBased on this reasoning, the statement "Gary is quiet" is false.\n\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
