he rabbit, but it does not directly indicate any visitation.\n\n6.**The rabbit visits the bear**:.\n   - This indicates that the rabbit has visited the bear.\n\n7.**The squirrel eats the cow**:.\n   - This indicates that the squirrel has eaten the cow.\n\n8.**The squirrel visits the rabbit**:.\n   - This indicates that the squirrel has visited the rabbit.\n\n9.**If someone visits the squirrel and the squirrel chases the cow then the cow is round**:.\n   - This is a conditional statement, but it does not directly relate to the bear\'s visit to the rabbit.\n\n10.**If someone is big and red then they chase the rabbit**:.\n    - This is a conditional statement, but it does not directly relate to the bear\'s visit to the rabbit.\n\n11.**If someone visits the rabbit then the rabbit visits the bear**:.\n    - This is a conditional statement, but it does not directly relate to the bear\'s visit to the rabbit.\n\n12.If no one chases the squirrel, then the squirrel does not eat the rabbit.\n    - This is an absolute statement that directly contradicts the bear\'s visit to the rabbit.\n\n13.**If someone eats the cow and the cow eats the rabbit then the cow chases the rabbit**:.\n    - This is a conditional statement, but it does not directly relate to the bear\'s visit to the rabbit.\n\n14.**If the squirrel chases the cow and the cow is round then the cow is young**:.\n    - This is a conditional statement, but it does not directly relate to the bear\'s visit to the rabbit.\n\n15.**If someone chases the squirrel then the squirrel eats the rabbit**:.\n    - This is a conditional statement, but it does not directly relate to the bear\'s visit to the rabbit.\n\n16.**If someone eats the bear then they chase the cow**.\n    - This is a conditional statement, but it does not directly relate to the bear\'s visit to the rabbit.\n\nFrom the given information, we have clear contradictions and no logical links that suggest the bear\'s visit to the rabbit. The actions of the bear and the 