messages:   82%|########2 | 495/600 [18:58<00:14,  7.04it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is cold. Anne is furry. Anne is rough. Anne is smart. Anne is white. Bob is nice. Bob is rough. Erin is cold. Erin is furry. Erin is nice. Erin is rough. Erin is smart. Erin is white. Erin is young. Fiona is cold. Fiona is furry. All smart things are cold. If Bob is young and Bob is cold then Bob is furry. Young things are cold. If Fiona is rough and Fiona is cold then Fiona is smart. Cold, furry things are white. All rough, nice things are young. If something is white and furry then it is smart.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Fiona is not young.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>.\nTo determine if the statement "Fiona is not young" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context, we need to carefully analyze the information provided and apply logical reasoning step by step.\n\n1.**Identify relevant information about Fiona:**.\n   - Fiona is cold.\n   - Fiona is furry.\n   - Fiona is rough.\n   - Fiona is smart.\n   - Fiona is white.\n\n2.**Analyze the given logical statements:**.\n   - "All smart things are cold.".\n   - "If Bob is young and Bob is cold then Bob is furry.".\n   - "Young things are cold.".\n   - "If Fiona is rough and Fiona is cold then Fiona is smart.".\n   - "Cold, furry things are white.".\n   - "All rough, nice things are young.".\n   - "If something is white and furry then it is smart.".\n\n3.**Check if Fiona is young:**.\n   - From the statement "All rough, nice things are young," we need to determine if Fiona is nice.\n   - From the statement "If something is white and furry then it is smart," we know Fiona is smart.\n   - Since Fiona is white and furry, by the given statement, Fiona is smart.\n   - However, the statement "All rough, nice things are young" does not directly apply to Fiona because we do not know if Fiona is nice.\nBased on the information provided, it is unclear whether Fiona is not young.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
