en.\n   - The statement "All quiet things are green" is given, but this doesn\'t directly apply to Fiona since we don\'t know her quiet status.\nFiona\'s Status:\n   - We know Fiona is quiet.\n   - We know Fiona is not white (from the context).\n\nConclusion:\n   - The statement "If Fiona is white and Fiona is green then Fiona is not quiet" is directly applicable because we don\'t know if Fiona is green.\n   - Since we know Fiona is not white and we don\'t have any information that confirms her being white, we can conclude that the statement "Fiona is not white" is false based on the given information.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n<answer>. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
